# DROP PROCEDURE / DROP FUNCTION ... IF EXISTS.
#
# The engine has no stored routines, so a `DROP {PROCEDURE|FUNCTION} IF EXISTS
# name` can never find one to drop -- and `IF EXISTS` makes that succeed silently
# (MySQL only attaches a note). It is the standard "drop before create" preamble
# in mysqldump output and migration scripts. The front-end parser has no stored-
# routine statements, so it rejected these outright; the server now answers the
# `IF EXISTS` form as a no-op OK.
#
# Expected to pass against both turso-mysql-server and a real mysqld.

# The IF EXISTS form succeeds even though no such routine exists.
statement ok
DROP PROCEDURE IF EXISTS noproc_demo

statement ok
DROP FUNCTION IF EXISTS nofunc_demo

# A schema-qualified name is accepted too.
statement ok
DROP PROCEDURE IF EXISTS conformance.noproc_demo

# mysqldump wraps the drop in a version-gated executable comment; the server
# unwraps it before dispatch, so it is the same no-op.
statement ok
/*!50003 DROP PROCEDURE IF EXISTS dumped_demo */

# Without IF EXISTS the statement fails on both: MySQL because the routine does
# not exist, the front-end because it does not implement stored routines.
statement error
DROP PROCEDURE noproc_demo

statement error
DROP FUNCTION nofunc_demo
